---
.PP
.SH "SAFETY GUARANTEES & CONTRACT"
1. \fBSurgical API Upgrades Only:\fR Only retired and deprecated Kubernetes API groups are upgraded to their stable successors (\fBapps/v1\fR, \fBnetworking.k8s.io/v1\fR, \fBbatch/v1\fR).
.PP
2. \fBZero Unsolicited Mutation:\fR No automated probe injection, container limits alteration, or label mutator runs during \fBmigrate\fR.
.PP
3. \fBMulti-Document & CRLF Preservation:\fR Multi-document YAML streams separated by \fB---\fR are migrated document-by-document, preserving document boundaries, comments, and Windows (\fB\r\n\fR) or Unix (\fB\n\fR) line endings.
.PP
4. \fBPre-Write Verification Gates:\fR Every migrated manifest must pass syntax validation, comment invariance, non-empty AST check, and OpenAPI schema verification before disk mutation.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "BACKUP & VERSION CONTROL BEST PRACTICES"
.IP "\(bu" 2
**Explicit \fB.bak\fR Safety Suffix:** When \fB--apply\fR runs without \fB--no-backup\fR, yamlr creates a safety snapshot named \fB<filename>.bak\fR (for example, \fBdeploy.yaml.bak\fR, never \fBdeploy.bak.yaml\fR). This intentional suffix naming ensures directory-level Kubernetes tools (e.g., \fBkubectl apply -f .\fR) will not parse or deploy the backup copy.
.IP "\(bu" 2
**Recommended \fB.gitignore\fR:** Add \fB*.bak\fR to your project's \fB.gitignore\fR to prevent accidentally committing local backup snapshots.
.IP "\(bu" 2
**CI/CD & GitOps Workflows:** In continuous integration and automated GitOps pipelines where full version history is maintained in Git, pass \fB--no-backup\fR to keep workspaces clean without generating snapshot files.
